              "fill": "$text-muted",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "A domain label sits at the popover's foot and names the mechanism the slider drives: DEVICE (kAudioDevicePropertyVolumeScalar while hogged — the DAC's own attenuator, full-scale samples on the wire) or SOFTWARE (engine gain, cubic taper). The % readout renders in the quality green when the path is transparent — unity software gain or device volume — and returns to text-primary below unity. On the bit-perfect engine with no hardware volume the slider is disabled at 100% with the domain label reading FIXED. Devices page: a device's class line appends \"Device volume\" when hardware volume is available while hogged (feature 31 phase 3 fills the Matrix's actual camp). Copy rule: \"samples leave Pulse untouched\", never \"bit-perfect to the DAC\" — the bit-perfect wording belongs to the integer engine's indicator alone (feature 32).",
