        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "PAO7t",
          "name": "Board Note",
          "fill": "$text-secondary",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Feature 32 (Jason, 2026-08-31 — supersedes feature 08's separate Exclusive toggle): one per-device Output mode control — Shared / Exclusive / Bit-perfect — one axis: shared AUHAL, hogged AUHAL, hogged integer. Stored mode None = AUTO, resolving down the ladder: gate passes → Bit-perfect; integer physical formats but gated transport or refused virtual → Exclusive; float-only → Shared. Pinning any segment drops the AUTO tag (Reset to Auto returns). The Bit-perfect segment is disabled with the NO INTEGER PATH tag on gated devices. Maps 1:1 onto the engine protocol: Shared → Universal{shared}, Exclusive → Universal{exclusive}, Bit-perfect → BitPerfect — no controller changes. Migration: stored exclusive_mode_override + engine collapse into one stored mode. Changing the active device's mode restarts playback; bit-perfect wording stays gated on the stage 5 DoP pass.",
          "lineHeight": 1.45,
          "fontFamily": "$font-sans",
          "fontSize": 11,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
