              "name": "Caption",
              "fill": "$text-secondary",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "Gate = transport + format (stage 1 findings): display and Bluetooth transports are excluded even when they advertise integer physical formats — the DELLs accept integer physical yet refuse every integer virtual write — and built-in output falls out by float-only formats. Bit-perfect segment disabled with the NO INTEGER PATH tag; AUTO still resolves Shared vs Exclusive per feature 08's ladder (this DELL: integer formats → Exclusive). Start-time virtual refusal (noErr, then settle timeout up to 2 s) is the backstop: clear error, never a silent float fallback.",
              "lineHeight": 1.45,
              "fontFamily": "$font-sans",
              "fontSize": 11,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
